      "message": "[Documentation](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/flash.h;l\u003d209-215;drc\u003d3bbdefd678ce52d8f7672b0189ba88972a64dfde) says that any positive return value means that the region is protected. Unfortunately [EC_ERROR_* codes are positive](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/common.h;l\u003d359;drc\u003d9c9df9c7d40daf7f77f8b4132aa959ab024b219c) which means that error from `check_prot_reg()` will be interpreted as enabled protection.\n\nI believe, this is a problem with `check_prot_reg()` it should return 0 if it\u0027s not possible to determine if the region is protected.\n\nAlso, `check_prot_reg()` returns that the region is protected even if it\u0027s only partially protected. It\u0027s good for checking before writing/erasing, but I\u0027m not sure if it\u0027s good here.",
